  <data name="msg_help_content_2_10" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>10, ρ: the correlation coefficient of random variables X and Y. Input combined with a matrix of 2 rows and N columns, such as "ρ(1,2,3,4,,5,6,7,8)", which means the correlation coefficient when X is 1, 2, 3, 4, and Y is 5, 6, 7, 8.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="msg_help_content_2_8" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>8, Dx: number of several variance. Input combined with matrix form, for example "d (1,2,3,4)" means 1, 2, 3 and 4 of the variance.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="msg_help_content_2_9" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>9, Cov: the covariance of random variables X and Y. Input combined with a matrix of 2 rows and N columns, such as "Cov(1,2,3,4,,5,6,7,8)", which means the covariance when X is 1, 2, 3, 4, and Y is 5, 6, 7, 8.</value>
