  </data>
  <data name="tooltip_npr.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>nPr: permutations, "A nPr B" represents the number of ways of obtaining an ordered subset of B elements from a set of A elements</value>
  </data>
  <data name="tooltip_rank.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>rank: used for matrices, such as "r(6,2,,3,1)", which means the rank of a matrix (6,2,,3,1)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="tooltip_rho.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ρ: the correlation coefficient of random variables X and Y. Input combined with a matrix of 2 rows and N columns, such as "ρ(1,2,3,4,,5,6,7,8)", which means the correlation coefficient when X is 1, 2, 3, 4, and Y is 5, 6, 7, 8</value>
  </data>
  <data name="tooltip_t.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>T: used for matrices, such as "(6,2,,3,1)^T", which means the transpose of a matrix (6,2,,3,1)</value>
